# core/inventory - What is actually loaded?
#
# Answers: which named graphs are present, which types occur in each, and how
# many distinct subjects carry each type.
#
# Does NOT prove: that the dataset is complete. A count far below expectation is
# usually a partial export rather than a small enterprise.
#
# Run this first, every session. An empty graph and a graph with no matching
# elements look identical from any later query, and only this one can tell them
# apart.
#
# Deliberately unscoped - {{GRAPH_OPEN:any}} rather than :semantic - because
# reporting which graphs exist is the job. A views graph is absent whenever the
# source carried no diagrams, and that absence is a finding worth seeing here
# rather than discovering three queries later.
{{PREFIXES}}
SELECT {{GRAPH_VAR:any}} ?type (COUNT(DISTINCT ?s) AS ?count)
WHERE {
  {{GRAPH_OPEN:any}}
    ?s a ?type .
  {{GRAPH_CLOSE}}
}
GROUP BY {{GRAPH_VAR:any}} ?type
ORDER BY {{GRAPH_VAR:any}} DESC(?count)
LIMIT {{LIMIT}}
